      "message": "because the @MEMOIZE, uses the parameters signature to generate the key for the map where it stores the cache. As we changed the signature to use a user object, this was causing more problems than helping; even though the attributes we use are the same (inside the user object), sometimes we might have more or less attributes there, and this would lead the method \"_shadow_federated_user\" to not work properly.\n\nThis process is not a very recurrent one; I mean, it is not execute for a user e every minute or so. Therefore, the use of @MEMOIZE does not seem to bring much benefits.",
